Notebook[{Cell["Verification", "ObjectName"], Cell["Verification sets how a \
calculation checks its result: Automatic (the usual checks), \"Exact\", \
\"Numerical\" (checks at WorkingPrecision) or None (no checks; the result is \
marked \"Unverified\"). Its session default (ConfigureVVMFTool) is the CG \
family's.", "Usage"], Cell["Status: Alpha.", "Notes"], 
  Cell["Option of the CG family (CGCoefficients, CacheCG, ValidateCG and the \
functions built on CG coefficients), of the Validate functions and of the \
Wolfram calculations that check their results (Phase 2C), and a session \
default of ConfigureVVMFTool for CGCoefficients and CacheCG: how a result is \
checked. Automatic (default) checks exactly for exact arithmetic and \
numerically for numerical arithmetic. \"Exact\" requires exact checks (with \
numerical data it is InapplicableOption). \"Numerical\" checks the identities \
on N[] at WorkingPrecision. None skips the checks of results (input, \
structural and positivity checks always run) and marks the result \
\"Unverified\".", "Notes"], Cell["Automatic, \"Exact\", \"Numerical\" or None \
(the Validate functions: Automatic, \"Exact\" or \"Numerical\"; the \
modular-form functions have no \"Exact\" route).", "Notes"], 
  Cell["Every stored CG entry carries a VerificationStatus, \"Exact\", \
\"Numerical\" or \"Unverified\", that is saved with the group; CGData reports \
it per target (\"Provenance\") and overall (\"VerificationStatus\"), and \
CGCacheInformation counts it per pair. A later call at a higher level checks \
a weaker stored entry and raises its status, or recomputes and replaces it \
when the check fails; a call with None serves stored entries as they are. The \
functions built on CG coefficients (TensorProductVectors, Contractions, \
CGPolynomialResult, TensorProductWeightedVectors, \
ModularTensorProductVectors, ModularContractions) pass their Verification to \
the inner CG call; its default there is plain Automatic, not the session's CG \
value. A call whose level asks for more than its input representations are \
verified at serves its result at their status and says so in one notice. The \
package library holds exactly verified coefficients only.", "Notes"], 
  Cell["Every record carries a verification status, the weakest of its own \
check and its inputs (Phase 2C): CG coefficients are served at the weakest of \
their own check, the participating representation variants and the group \
(Provenance \"Verification\"; \"CheckStatus\" is the entry's own check); \
vector records, contraction sets, model terms and models, mass matrices and \
modular forms follow the same rule; RepresentationView shows the status \
column when a stored variant is weaker than Exact.", "Notes"], 
  Cell["The switch on other calculations (Phase 2C-ii): \
ValidateRepresentation, ValidateModel, ValidateMassMatrix, \
ValidateModularModel (the level of their checks), ValidateModularForm \
(Automatic or \"Numerical\"); UnitarizeRepresentation, \
DiagonalizeRepresentationT, DecomposeRepresentation (result identities; their \
Validation records \"VerificationStatus\" and \"NotChecked\" for skipped \
checks); AddModelTerm and AddModularFormCouplings (covariance; None adds \
unchecked terms whose Symmetry is \"Unchecked\"; a later ValidateModel checks \
them, bounded by their sources); BindModularForms (the Stage 7 validation of \
each form); ConstructModularForms (recipe evidence); SolveModularCoefficients \
and ModularFormGetCoeff (None: ProofStatus \"Unchecked\"); ImportModelData \
(the archive's model and matrices; None keeps a registered export's recorded \
statuses and makes any other file \"Unverified\"). The export ledger records \
the weakest record of every saved file, and model archives record weak term \
and model statuses. Functions without a result check of their own carry their \
inputs' statuses: CreateModel, CreateModularModel, CoupleContractions, \
CoupleExpressions, ImportModularFormData (structural checks only), the \
extraction and evaluation functions.", "Notes"], 
  Cell["Representations (Phase 2C-iii): ComputeGroupRepresentations at None \
has GAP match class traces only and stores each new variant as an inert \
record with status \"Unverified\" (no GAP unitarization runs); at \
\"Numerical\" each one is then checked on N[] in Wolfram and stored again at \
\"Numerical\". SetGroupRepresentation, ChangeGroupRepBasis and \
TransformGroupRepresentations (Wolfram route) at \"Numerical\" or None store \
inert records with that status. GAP never holds an unverified variant \
natively: weak variants are inert there, never outrank a verified one and \
never satisfy a full-level request (a later full request computes verified \
variants, which become active). ValidateRepresentation[g, id] stores a \
verified copy of a weak active variant (same matrices and identity) and makes \
it active (write-back). A variant's status is not part of the context \
identity, so raising it keeps every context, vector and model built before.", 
   "Notes"], Cell["Groups (Phase 2C-iii): BuildGroup, BuildGroupFromGAP and \
BuildModularGroup take Verification. At \"Numerical\" GAP computes the \
characters and their class transport without its consistency proof (the row \
comparison and orthogonality), and Wolfram checks orthogonality, degrees and \
integrality numerically: the group's status is \"Numerical\". At None nothing \
is checked: \"Unverified\" (BuildModularGroup and AssignModularGenerators at \
None also skip the S,T proof; AssignModularGenerators has no \"Numerical\"). \
The representations a weak build computes are weak too. Every record derived \
from a weak group is bounded by its status. ValidateGroup raises it. \
ImportGroupData and LoadGroup: a registered file (the user's export ledger or \
the package library) imports at its recorded level without re-checking \
anything (its CG coefficients keep their recorded statuses); \"Exact\" \
re-checks it in GAP (LoadGroup then loads a new copy); an unregistered file \
at Automatic or \"Exact\" is re-proved in GAP, at \"Numerical\" or None it \
imports without GAP, with its claims weakened to what was checked: \
\"Numerical\" when only its character table is checked numerically, \
\"Unverified\" at None or when it holds an S,T assignment, representations, a \
generator presentation certificate or element words (no numerical check \
exists for them); receipt \"UnverifiedImport\". The numerical check covers \
the character table only: such a group's order and GAP ID are the file's \
claims until ValidateGroup proves them, and its subgroup lists are not \
imported (GroupSubgroups recomputes them). Ordinary operations never raise \
such a group; ValidateGroup proves it. GroupSubgroups, \
NormalSubgroupsByIndex, GroupElementWords and CheckGeneratorMap are exact by \
construction (\"Numerical\" is InapplicableOption). The package library holds \
exactly verified groups only.", "Notes"], Cell["See Also", "SeeAlsoSection"], 
  Cell[TextData[{ButtonBox["CGCoefficients", BaseStyle -> "Hyperlink", 
      ButtonData -> {"CGCoefficients.nb", None}], "  |  ", 
     ButtonBox["CacheCG", BaseStyle -> "Hyperlink", 
      ButtonData -> {"CacheCG.nb", None}], "  |  ", 
     ButtonBox["ValidateCG", BaseStyle -> "Hyperlink", 
      ButtonData -> {"ValidateCG.nb", None}], "  |  ", 
     ButtonBox["FieldMethod", BaseStyle -> "Hyperlink", 
      ButtonData -> {"FieldMethod.nb", None}], "  |  ", 
     ButtonBox["CGCacheInformation", BaseStyle -> "Hyperlink", 
      ButtonData -> {"CGCacheInformation.nb", None}], "  |  ", 
     ButtonBox["ValidateModel", BaseStyle -> "Hyperlink", 
      ButtonData -> {"ValidateModel.nb", None}], "  |  ", 
     ButtonBox["UnitarizeRepresentation", BaseStyle -> "Hyperlink", 
      ButtonData -> {"UnitarizeRepresentation.nb", None}], "  |  ", 
     ButtonBox["AddModelTerm", BaseStyle -> "Hyperlink", 
      ButtonData -> {"AddModelTerm.nb", None}], "  |  ", 
     ButtonBox["LoadGroup", BaseStyle -> "Hyperlink", 
      ButtonData -> {"LoadGroup.nb", None}]}], "SeeAlso"], 
  Cell["Examples Initialization", "ExamplesInitializationSection"], 
  Cell["Open this notebook in its repository location. GAP must be installed; \
LINS is required for its bounded search page. Evaluate the setup before the \
examples.", "ExampleText"], 
  Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{RowBox[{"Get", "[", RowBox[{"FileNameJoin", "[", 
          RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{RowBox[{"Nest", "[", RowBox[{"DirectoryName", 
                  ",", RowBox[{"NotebookFileName", "[", "]"}], ",", "5"}], 
                "]"}], ",", "\"Kernel\"", ",", "\"init.m\""}], "}"}], "]"}], 
        "]"}], ";"}]], "ExampleInitialization"], 
  Cell["Basic Examples", "PrimaryExamplesSection"], 
  Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
      RowBox[{RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{RowBox[{"g", "=", RowBox[{"BuildGroup", 
                "[", RowBox[{RowBox[{"GroupPresentation", "[", RowBox[
                     {RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"\"s\"", ",", "\"t\""}], "}"}], 
                      ",", RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"\"s^2\"", ",", "\"t^2\"", 
                          ",", "\"(s.t)^3\""}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", 
                  RowBox[{"StoreGAPState", "\[Rule]", "False"}]}], "]"}]}], 
            ",", "d"}], "}"}], ",", RowBox[
         {RowBox[{"d", "=", RowBox[{"First", "[", RowBox[{"Select", "[", 
                RowBox[{RowBox[{"g", "[", "\"IrrepOrder\"", "]"}], ",", 
                  RowBox[{RowBox[{RowBox[{"RepDim", "[", RowBox[
                         {"GroupRepresentation", "[", RowBox[{"g", ",", 
                          "#1"}], "]"}], "]"}], "===", "2"}], "&"}]}], "]"}], 
              "]"}]}], ";", RowBox[{"Block", "[", 
            RowBox[{RowBox[{"{", "Print", "}"}], ",", RowBox[{"{", 
                RowBox[{RowBox[{RowBox[{"First", "[", RowBox[
                       {"CGCoefficients", "[", RowBox[{"g", ",", RowBox[
                          {"{", RowBox[{"d", ",", "d"}], "}"}], ",", "d", 
                          ",", RowBox[{"Verification", "\[Rule]", "None"}]}], 
                        "]"}], "]"}], "[", "\"VerificationStatus\"", "]"}], 
                  ",", RowBox[{RowBox[{"First", "[", RowBox[
                       {"CGCoefficients", "[", RowBox[{"g", ",", RowBox[
                          {"{", RowBox[{"d", ",", "d"}], "}"}], ",", "d"}], 
                        "]"}], "]"}], "[", "\"VerificationStatus\"", "]"}]}], 
                "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]], "Input", 
   CellTags -> "VerifiedExample"], 
  Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"\"Unverified\"", ",", "\"Exact\""}], 
      "}"}]], "Output"], Cell["Possible Issues", "ExampleSection"], 
  Cell["Invalid input returns a structured Failure. Check FailureQ before \
using the result.", "ExampleText"], 
  Cell[BoxData[RowBox[{"FailureQ", "[", RowBox[{"CGCoefficients", "[", 
        RowBox[{"\"no group\"", ",", RowBox[{"{", RowBox[{"\"a\"", ",", 
              "\"b\""}], "}"}], ",", RowBox[{"Verification", "\[Rule]", 
            "\"Sometimes\""}]}], "]"}], "]"}]], "Input", 
   CellTags -> "VerifiedErrorExample"], Cell[BoxData["True"], "Output"], 
  Cell["Related Guides", "MoreAboutSection"], 
  Cell[TextData[{ButtonBox["Constructing finite groups", 
      BaseStyle -> "Hyperlink", ButtonData -> 
       {"../../Tutorials/ConstructingFiniteGroups.nb", None}]}], 
   "MoreAbout"], Cell[CellGroupData[{Cell["Metadata", "MetadataSection"], 
     Cell["Symbol", "Categorization", CellLabel -> "Entity Type"], 
     Cell["VVMFTool", "Categorization", CellLabel -> "Paclet Name"], 
     Cell["VVMFTool`", "Categorization", CellLabel -> "Context"], 
     Cell["VVMFTool/ref/Verification", "Categorization", 
      CellLabel -> "URI"]}, Closed]]}, 
 WindowTitle -> "Verification \[LongDash] VVMFTool", 
 WindowSize -> {1000, 850}, TaggingRules -> <|"Paclet" -> "VVMFTool", 
   "Status" -> "Alpha"|>, StyleDefinitions -> FrontEnd`FileName[{"Wolfram"}, 
   "FunctionPageStylesExt.nb", CharacterEncoding -> "UTF-8"]]
